My brain is getting all tangled up, but dot-haride dot-com.

116
00:23:27,588 --> 00:23:30,168
あっちゃっちゃっちゃ パリパリ エブリバディ
Ah-cha-cha-cha, crispy crispy, everybody.

117
00:23:30,308 --> 00:23:32,498
『魔王はおやつに入りません』
"The Demon King is not included in the snacks."

118
00:23:33,188 --> 00:23:36,368
ドットハライド ドットコム あっちゃっちゃっちゃ
Dot-haride dot-com, ah-cha-cha-cha.

119
00:23:36,528 --> 00:23:39,648
ドンシャリドンシャリ エブリバディ
Don-shari don-shari, everybody.

120
00:23:39,778 --> 00:23:42,238
愛のいないないない
Love is nowhere to be found.

121
00:23:54,018 --> 00:23:59,348
エットセットライヘンバッハから 凄腕探偵さん 続いてご歓談
From Etset Reichenbach, a top-tier detective follows with pleasant conversation.

122
00:23:59,848 --> 00:24:07,008
ﾎﾘｴﾝﾄ 9号車 の窓 あの怪盗達が幕と引くという
The window of Horient Car 9, where those phantom thieves draw the curtain.

123
00:24:07,478 --> 00:24:12,798
孤高にいく二人 海の原 囁き暗号 無視したの
Two people going in isolation across the ocean expanse, whispering codes, did you ignore them?

124
00:24:13,868 --> 00:24:20,278
ABCどっかエビすだか でも運動ちゃんとしてね
ABC somewhere, Ebisu perhaps, but make sure you get proper exercise!

125
00:24:21,228 --> 00:24:27,258
甲が乙を隠す そんじゃご参戦 監視キッサン お疲れさん
甲 hides 乙. Well then, participation by 監視キッサン, good work.

126
00:24:27,978 --> 00:24:34,098
四捨五入やってみな 四捨五入人どこ行った？ 謎解きはまだまだ
Try rounding to the nearest whole number. Where did the rounded people go? The puzzle solving is still ongoing.

127
00:24:34,828 --> 00:24:39,528
そして誰もいなくなった 御珍になって おやめになって 大事件
And then there were none. Becoming precious, stopping that, a big incident.

128
00:24:39,898 --> 00:24:42,998
お下げ揺らす 探偵さん
The detective swaying their pigtails.

129
00:24:43,128 --> 00:24:47,268
六畳ベーベ ガストンベーベ いかないで and more
Six-tatami Bebe, Gaston Bebe, don't go, and more.

130
00:24:47,668 --> 00:24:54,628
先生の意地悪はマイルド ドットハライド ドットコム あっちゃっちゃっちゃ
The teacher's teasing is mild. Dot-haride dot-com, ah-cha-cha-cha.

131
00:24:54,718 --> 00:24:58,958
パリパリ エブリバディ 魔王はおやつに入りません
Crispy crispy, everybody. The Demon King is not included in the snacks.

132
00:25:00,706 --> 00:25:02,806
Everybody Alibi ない ない ない
Everybody, alibi, none, none, none

133
00:25:18,006 --> 00:25:24,006
怪盗・令嬢の罠にハマり 次々と姿を消していく 名探偵たち
Falling into the phantom thief and young lady's trap, detectives disappear one after another.

134
00:25:24,706 --> 00:25:30,206
そして 探偵のいる間に 人々の心は 密室となった
And while the detectives were there, people's hearts became a locked room.

135
00:25:32,506 --> 00:25:36,606
「でも、それならどうして私だけが無事だったのでしょうか？」
"But if so, why was only I safe?"

136
00:25:37,106 --> 00:25:41,606
「その答えは一つしか考えられない。と……言うと？」
"That can only mean one thing. You mean...?"

137
00:25:42,506 --> 00:25:46,206
「あまりに無能すぎるがゆえに、キミは探偵として感情にも入れられていなかったのだ！」
"Because you are far too incompetent, you weren't even considered a detective emotionally!"

138
00:25:46,706 --> 00:25:50,506
「――リーター！」
"--Liar!"

139
00:25:51,606 --> 00:25:57,406
およしになって おやめになって 飼い慣らす お下げ 揺らす 探偵さん
Cut it out, stop it, you detective who dangles and sways what you've tamed.

140
00:25:58,406 --> 00:26:04,906
ロックンベイビー ガストンベイビー 行かないで おーのー ステイの 一番いけずジェネレーション ハックトニック 難事件 推理さかたの 先生
Rock 'n' baby, gaston baby, don't go, oh no, stay, the meanest generation, hack-tonic, difficult case, detective story author teacher.

141
00:26:12,606 --> 00:26:15,506
うーたらぱーたら うーたらぱーたら 言わないで あーおー
Don't go babbling on and on, ah-oh.

142
00:26:16,006 --> 00:26:26,006
まだまだこんがらがってきたけど 怖いかわいいや トリックあまいぜ 通りゃんせ 通りゃんせ
It's still getting all tangled up, but scary-cute, sweet tricks, Tourianse, Tourianse.

143
00:26:39,906 --> 00:26:47,006
小さい2人の子供が約束した ずっといっしょに笑っていようの約束
Two small children made a promise—a promise to always laugh together.

144
00:26:47,906 --> 00:26:56,106
今もなお ２人の絆は確かなもので 友情と愛情が織りなす素敵な物語
Even now, the bond between the two remains steadfast, a wonderful tale woven by friendship and affection.

145
00:26:57,506 --> 00:27:05,106
あははっ…なんでもないことに 妙にツボっちゃう時あるよねっ
Ahaha... You know how sometimes you just crack up over nothing at all.

146
00:27:15,606 --> 00:27:19,106
あー恋に落ちた舞うら 咲き止まないや
Ah—the swirling fall of love just won't stop blossoming.

147
00:27:19,606 --> 00:27:22,906
何度もめくって 心をかし
Turning the pages over and over, playing with our hearts.

148
00:27:23,606 --> 00:27:27,106
泣いてばっかりだったの それがどうだい 今や
We used to do nothing but cry, but look at us now.

149
00:27:27,606 --> 00:27:29,806
腹捩るくらい笑う
Laughing until our stomachs hurt.

150
00:27:30,506 --> 00:27:33,506
ずっと一緒に笑う
Laughing together, forever.

151
00:27:34,506 --> 00:27:41,806
きみが持ってる白い花に あたし見合わない 悲しくなる 無垢な恋とか正しさとか
I don't measure up to the white flower you hold, making me sad; innocent love, righteousness—

152
00:27:45,506 --> 00:27:48,806
誰も教えてくれないかった
No one ever taught us any of it.

153
00:27:49,506 --> 00:27:56,106
昨日会ったばっかで 今日もどっか会えたら なんて思う暮らし 慎ましいくらいだよね
Just met yesterday, hoping we can run into each other somewhere today—such a life is almost modest.

154
00:27:56,606 --> 00:28:02,106
全部許されたの びっくりしちゃってさ 涙あふれてたよ
Finding out everything was forgiven took me by surprise, and tears overflowed.

155
00:28:04,906 --> 00:28:11,506
もう愛になる花歌 透き通った空に 手を繋いでった 夢のしるし
A flower song turning into love, holding hands beneath a clear sky, the proof of a dream.

156
00:28:12,506 --> 00:28:16,206
どんな前世だってさ 忘れたっていいんだ きみと笑えるなら
Whatever past life it was, it's fine to forget it, as long as I can laugh with you.

157
00:28:19,906 --> 00:28:22,806
心が触れるたび 綺麗な音鳴る
Every time our hearts touch, a beautiful sound rings out.

158
00:28:23,506 --> 00:28:26,506
目と目が合ってくすぐたいね
Our eyes meet, and it tickles so.

159
00:28:27,506 --> 00:28:30,106
なんでもないこと 妙にツボるね
We mysteriously crack up over nothing at all.

160
00:28:30,906 --> 00:28:36,806
全部教えてくれて ありがとう
Thank you for teaching me everything.

161
00:28:49,506 --> 00:29:03,806
きみが持ってる白い花を あたしの紅色と合わせたら 霜が溶けては雲がゆく もう寒くないよ
If you match the white flower you hold with my crimson, frost melts, clouds pass, and it's no longer cold.

162
00:29:09,506 --> 00:29:12,806
あー恋に落ちた舞うら 咲き止まないや
Ah—the swirling fall of love just won't stop blossoming.

163
00:29:13,506 --> 00:29:16,506
何度もめくって 心をかし
Turning the pages over and over, playing with our hearts.

164
00:29:17,106 --> 00:29:20,106
泣いてばっかりだったの それがどうだい 今や
We used to do nothing but cry, but look at us now.

165
00:29:20,906 --> 00:29:23,106
腹捩るくらい笑う
Laughing until our stomachs hurt.

166
00:29:23,906 --> 00:29:30,506
ずっと一緒に笑って 心をかし
Laughing together forever, playing with our hearts.

167
00:29:37,506 --> 00:29:42,806
ずっと一緒に笑う 最後の日を笑う
Laughing together forever, laughing on our final day.

168
00:29:55,506 --> 00:30:01,106
これは 遠い遠い 名も知らぬ世界で、
This is a tale in a far, far, unknown world...

169
00:30:26,020 --> 00:30:31,920
遠い遠い時の果て そこに住む人は皆
At the end of time, far, far away, everyone living there

170
00:30:31,920 --> 00:30:38,160
永遠の命をもつ 世界での話
possesses eternal life—a tale of that world.

171
00:30:38,400 --> 00:30:44,920
赤い実の成る木の下 生まれながらに
Beneath the tree bearing red fruit, born with it from the very start—

172
00:30:44,920 --> 00:30:50,920
死の呪いがかけられた 少女の話
the story of a girl cursed with death.

173
00:31:00,680 --> 00:31:06,800
色付いた街外れ 青く光る後堂
On the outskirts of the colorful town, a blue-glowing back hall...

174
00:31:06,800 --> 00:31:13,040
赤い実のお菓子屋
A red-fruit sweet shop.

175
00:31:13,040 --> 00:31:19,040
ちょっぴり寒くなった 今日は妙に誇らしげ
It has grown a bit chilly today, yet she is strangely proud.

176
00:31:19,040 --> 00:31:25,840
自信作を売りに行く 待ってて 今度こそ 美味しいんだから
Off to sell her proudest creation. Just wait, this time it really is delicious!

177
00:31:26,840 --> 00:31:32,680
時計塔の見える市 珍しく賑やかね
The market visible from the clock tower is unusually bustling.

178
00:31:32,680 --> 00:31:38,440
La La Lu La Lucky!! 物憂げな街の隅 ひとり
La La Lu La Lucky!! All alone in a melancholy corner of the town.

179
00:31:38,440 --> 00:31:44,160
赤い実のパイですか? 自信作なのよ
Would you like a red-fruit pie? It's my masterpiece!

180
00:31:44,160 --> 00:31:49,960
そんなのひとつも売れないさ
Not a single one of them will sell.

181
00:31:49,960 --> 00:31:56,320
少女を見て蔑む人達 みんなと何も変わらないのに
The people look down on the girl with scorn, even though she is no different from anyone else.

182
00:31:56,320 --> 00:32:02,320
美味しくできたのに 今日も声は届かないのね
Even though I made it so delicious, my voice still doesn't reach anyone today...

183
00:32:02,320 --> 00:32:07,960
まるで透明になったみたいだわ
It feels as though I've become completely invisible.

184
00:32:07,960 --> 00:32:13,960
そして誰もが知らぬふりをした 何故なら少女は呪われているから
And everyone pretended not to notice, because the girl is cursed.

185
00:32:13,960 --> 00:32:21,480
死んだ世界で呪いとひとり生きていた 少女の話
The story of a girl who lived alone with her curse in a dead world.

186
00:32:30,680 --> 00:32:37,040
夜なべでアレンジパイと ニッコリスマイル引っ提げ
Working through the night on a custom pie, flashing a cheerful smile,

187
00:32:37,040 --> 00:32:43,240
少女はまだ諦めない 時計塔の針も空を指して
the girl still hasn't given up. As the clock tower's hands point to the sky

188
00:32:43,240 --> 00:32:49,000
お腹も鳴るそんな時 ふと後ろから一人が少女を押す
and her stomach starts to rumble, suddenly someone pushes her from behind.

189
00:32:49,000 --> 00:32:54,960
甘いカゴは落ちる お菓子を踏み行く人達 平気な顔してさ
Her sweet basket falls. People trample over the treats with unconcerned faces.

190
00:32:54,960 --> 00:33:01,680
惨めに拾い集める ふとひとりの手が
As she miserably gathers them up, suddenly, a hand...

191
00:33:01,680 --> 00:33:13,960
ドロドロのパイを口に入れ 「おいしいね」
takes a muddy, mashed-up pie into its mouth and says, "It's delicious."

192
00:33:14,680 --> 00:33:21,440
その声で心は溢れた まるで輪郭を描いたみたいだわ
At those words, her heart overflowed, as if an outline had finally been drawn for her.

193
00:33:23,640 --> 00:33:30,560
そして彼は手を差し出した 何故なら少女に呪われているから
And then he reached out his hand, because he, too, is cursed just like the girl.

194
00:33:31,680 --> 00:33:40,840
死んだ世界でただ二人生きていた 遠い物語
A distant tale of just two people living together in a dead world.

195
00:33:51,800 --> 00:33:57,880
街の人達は憐れむ 赤い実食べて呪われたもの
The townspeople pity those cursed for eating the red fruit,

196
00:33:57,880 --> 00:34:03,840
永遠に生きれずに死ぬのさ 鳴き呼んで可哀想な話
dying without living forever—a crying, pitiful tale.

197
00:34:08,800 --> 00:34:14,880
二人は笑う それでも笑う
The two of them laugh. Even so, they laugh.

198
00:34:14,880 --> 00:34:21,440
La La La とっても素敵な呪いだね
La La La, what a truly wonderful curse it is.

199
00:34:21,440 --> 00:34:31,960
例え明日死んでも 『今』が確実で大切になるから
Even if we die tomorrow, because 'now' is certain and precious to us.

200
00:34:35,680 --> 00:34:42,000
もう声は届かないのね まるで透明になったみたいだわ
My voice still doesn't reach anyone... as though I've become completely invisible.

201
00:34:44,680 --> 00:34:50,960
そして誰もが知らぬふりをした 何故なら世界が呪われているから
And everyone pretended not to notice, because the world itself is cursed.

202
00:34:54,431 --> 00:34:58,641
『永遠』の呪いは解かれていた
The curse of 'eternity' had been broken,

203
00:34:58,641 --> 00:35:02,641
まるでふたりのほうが狂ったみたいだろう
as if the two of them were the ones who had gone mad.

204
00:35:02,841 --> 00:35:07,101
どうして いつか笑うように眠る
Why do they sleep hoping to smile one day...

205
00:35:07,831 --> 00:35:11,031
何故なら二人も囚われてるから
Because both of them are trapped here.

206
00:35:11,861 --> 00:35:21,001
死んだ世界で二人だけが幸せだった
In this dead world, only the two of them were happy together.

207
00:36:14,472 --> 00:36:17,372
さて、今日はこれくらいにしておきましょう、
Now then, let's leave it at that for today.

208
00:36:17,722 --> 00:36:20,222
…そろそろ時間になりましたし
...It's almost time, after all.

209
00:36:20,672 --> 00:36:24,022
…え？どこへ向かうのかって？
...Eh? Where are we heading, you ask?

210
00:36:25,222 --> 00:36:28,222
今日は何の日かご存知ないのですか？
Do you not know what day today is?

211
00:36:29,622 --> 00:36:35,022
今日は、この王国の地下深くにある冥界でのハロウィンパーティですよ！
Today is the Halloween party in the underworld, deep beneath this kingdom!

212
00:36:36,122 --> 00:36:40,572
死者と生者が楽しむ年に一度のお祭りです。
It's a once-a-year festival where the dead and the living celebrate together.

213
00:36:40,972 --> 00:36:43,072
さぁ、一緒に向かいましょう、
Now then, let's head there together.

214
00:36:44,922 --> 00:36:50,072
でも、気を付けて。パーティとはいえ、死者が争う冥界です。
But be careful. Though it's a party, it's an underworld where the dead struggle.

215
00:36:50,722 --> 00:36:55,522
誰かの思念や死者達によって奇妙な事が起こるかもしれません、
Strange things might happen due to someone's lingering thoughts or the dead,

216
00:36:56,322 --> 00:37:00,922
でも、決してそちらに耳を傾けすぎてはいけませんよ…
but you must never pay too much heed to them...

217
00:37:01,722 --> 00:37:03,522
それでは、参りましょう
Now then, let us go.

218
00:37:49,822 --> 00:37:52,722
誰かが言いました
Someone said...

219
00:37:53,322 --> 00:37:57,322
激しく燃えるものほど
The more intensely something burns,

220
00:37:57,822 --> 00:38:04,722
煌めく引き換えにその身をすぐ焦がし切ると
the quicker it scorches away its own body in exchange for that dazzling light.

221
00:38:12,722 --> 00:38:16,222
数ある炉台に
Upon countless hearths,

222
00:38:16,522 --> 00:38:20,222
お好きな火を灯しましょう
let us kindle whatever flame you desire.

223
00:38:20,722 --> 00:38:27,222
期待と裏腹に燃ればお生憎様
Despite your expectations, if it burns down, too bad for you.

224
00:38:27,722 --> 00:38:34,722
ランランランラン 右手には錆びた時計 左には油の筒
Run, run, run, run. In your right hand, a rusted clock; in your left, a cylinder of oil.

225
00:38:36,722 --> 00:38:42,222
猟のドレスを着飾って さぁ
Adorned in a hunting dress, now...

226
00:38:43,222 --> 00:38:50,222
激しく 儚く 青く燃ゆる花びら
Fiercely, fleetingly, flower petals burning blue,

227
00:38:50,722 --> 00:38:57,622
瞬き ゆらめく 生を彩り照らせ
twinkling, flickering, illuminating and coloring life,

228
00:38:57,722 --> 00:39:04,722
いずれ尽き果てる未来へと
toward a future that will eventually burn out to the end.

229
00:39:09,722 --> 00:39:16,522
ゆりかごの目の前で甘く飛び交う銃弾
Right before the cradle, bullets fly about sweetly.

230
00:39:17,522 --> 00:39:24,522
指だけ動かせば容易くその火は潰える
If you merely move your finger, that flame is easily extinguished.

231
00:39:39,722 --> 00:39:46,922
仮初の情熱で焼け爛れた舌では
With a tongue scorched and festered by transient passion,

232
00:39:47,722 --> 00:39:54,222
上手に喋ることができないようで
it seems you cannot speak properly,

233
00:39:54,722 --> 00:40:02,222
喉元過ぎても毒を孕ませて
harboring poison even after it passes the throat,

234
00:40:02,677 --> 00:40:09,677
やがては殻を腐らせるでしょう
Eventually, the shell will rot away...

235
00:40:10,677 --> 00:40:13,477
ランランランラン 揺らぐ死と生の狭間
Run, run, run, run... In the flickering space between life and death,

236
00:40:14,677 --> 00:40:17,177
焼ける心と歌う
I sing with a burning heart.

237
00:40:18,177 --> 00:40:23,677
描いた最愛の終焉を
Painting our most beloved end...

238
00:40:26,177 --> 00:40:32,677
激しく働く 蒼く燃える花びら
Working fiercely, blue-burning petals,

239
00:40:33,677 --> 00:40:40,677
瞬きゆらめく 生を彩り照らせ
Flickering and wavering, illuminate and color life,

240
00:40:41,677 --> 00:40:47,677
いずれ尽き果てるその先へ
Toward that place where they will eventually burn out.

241
00:41:04,477 --> 00:41:11,177
あちらの世界に引きずり込まれないうちに早く会場へ向かわないといけませんね、
We need to hurry to the venue before we get dragged into that world...

242
00:41:11,777 --> 00:41:13,877
気を付けてついてきてくださいね、
Please be careful and follow along.

243
00:41:14,477 --> 00:41:17,677
あまり深入りすると、おっと…
If you wander in too deep, well... oops...

244
00:41:18,677 --> 00:41:22,177
そうそう、知らない方がきっと懸命ですよ
That's right, it's definitely wiser not to know.

245
00:41:22,677 --> 00:41:27,177
なんだかすっごく心地が良いよね
Somehow it feels awfully comfortable, doesn't it?

246
00:41:39,677 --> 00:41:43,177
[Title: アメージングハッピーハロウィンナイト]
[Title: Amazing Happy Halloween Night]

247
00:41:44,477 --> 00:41:48,677
気付けば見知らぬ 世界に立っていた
Before I knew it, I was standing in an unfamiliar world.

248
00:41:49,477 --> 00:41:54,677
たったどこかも分からず 毎日毎日毎日泣いていた
Not even knowing where I was, I cried every single day,

249
00:41:54,777 --> 00:41:55,677
なんて暇もなく
without even having the time for that.

250
00:41:55,877 --> 00:41:57,277
おかしな面々が
A strange group of people

251
00:41:57,477 --> 00:41:59,177
おどけて転がるの
are tumbling around playfully.

252
00:41:59,477 --> 00:42:04,677
その馬鹿々しさに希望も恐怖もなくなった
In that absurdity, all hope and fear vanished.

253
