GIVE ME A CHERRY PIE, or else may I choke you up?

308
00:46:21,818 --> 00:46:25,118
GIVE ME A FLOWY DRESS それとも may I stab you to death?
GIVE ME A FLOWY DRESS, or else may I stab you to death?

309
00:46:26,118 --> 00:46:32,118
poison, rope, choking, knife, scissors, choose one...

310
00:46:32,618 --> 00:46:33,618
choose one!

311
00:46:35,118 --> 00:46:36,618
「さぁ選んで」
"Now, make your choice."

312
00:46:36,618 --> 00:46:37,918
なんちゃって ドッキリ大成功！
Just kidding, prank successfully pulled!

313
00:46:38,118 --> 00:46:42,118
響くパンパカパンファンファーレで にっこり笑ってはいピース
With a resounding fanfare, smile and say "peace"!

314
00:46:42,618 --> 00:46:44,618
あー怖かったななんて
Saying "Oh, that was scary,"

315
00:46:44,918 --> 00:46:48,118
座り込んで涙目で 笑う顔みたいな
sitting down in tears with a laughing face...

316
00:46:50,918 --> 00:46:53,618
ちっちゃな箱の中の モンスターに怯えるくらいなら
Rather than cowering in fear from the monster inside a tiny box,

317
00:46:53,918 --> 00:46:57,318
いつだってここにおいで もっとずっと本能的に楽しくなれるよ
come on over here anytime, and you can enjoy yourself much more instinctively!

318
00:47:01,918 --> 00:47:04,618
恐怖と踊っちゃおうぜ
Let's dance with fear!

319
00:47:05,118 --> 00:47:07,918
躁鬱相転移でキメてカタルシス
Clinch catharsis with manic-depressive phase transition,

320
00:47:08,118 --> 00:47:11,218
もういっちょ感情ジェットコースターで ご機嫌デトックス
and detox your mood with one more emotional roller coaster!

321
00:47:26,418 --> 00:47:29,618
満月が暴く醜悪な本性
The full moon exposes hideous true natures,

322
00:47:29,918 --> 00:47:33,218
デタラメに杖振り回し hocus pocus
swinging wands wildly, hocus pocus.

323
00:47:33,618 --> 00:47:37,018
劣等感を苗床に育つ呪いをどうぞ
Here is a curse grown from the seedbed of inferiority complex;

324
00:47:37,218 --> 00:47:39,918
摘み取る術を知っているかい？
do you know how to pluck it away?

325
00:47:40,618 --> 00:47:42,618
『迷える哀れな子羊たちよ』
"O stray, pitiful lambs,"

326
00:47:42,918 --> 00:47:45,918
『お菓子が欲しいかい？ それとも安らぎが欲しいかい？』
"do you want sweets? Or do you want peace?"

327
00:47:46,118 --> 00:47:49,918
『永遠に求め続けるの？ それならば、ずっと苦しいままだ』
"Will you keep seeking forever? If so, you will remain in eternal suffering."

328
00:47:50,118 --> 00:47:56,118
『恐怖からの解放によって、成し得る救いがあるのならば、この目隠しはそのままに』
"If there is salvation to be attained through liberation from fear, leaving this blindfold as it is..."

329
00:47:56,618 --> 00:47:58,618
『さぁ、イタズラ完了』
"Now, prank complete."

330
00:47:59,118 --> 00:48:02,118
永遠に断ち切れない 呪いの鎖にとらわれ
Trapped in the chains of an eternal, unbreakable curse,

331
00:48:02,318 --> 00:48:06,318
朽ち果ててしまう前に 震えあがって審判を前に
before you rot away, trembling before the judgment...

332
00:48:06,918 --> 00:48:10,318
悩みぞちょっと弄るだけであら不思議！
Just tinkering with your worries a little—oh how wondrous!

333
00:48:10,918 --> 00:48:15,618
こんなに気持ち良くて 気分爽快
It feels so good, feeling so refreshed!

334
00:48:19,118 --> 00:48:22,118
なんちゃって ドッキリ大成功！
Just kidding, prank successfully pulled!

335
00:48:22,318 --> 00:48:26,118
響くパンパカパンファンファーレで にっこり笑ってはいポーズ
With a resounding fanfare, smile and strike a pose!

336
00:48:26,318 --> 00:48:30,618
あー怖かったななんて へたり込んで涙目で
Saying "Oh, that was scary," collapsing in tears,

337
00:48:30,918 --> 00:48:33,618
笑う顔っていいな
a laughing face is wonderful.

338
00:48:34,118 --> 00:48:38,618
もう苦しまなくていいよ こんなに頑張ったんだから
You don't have to suffer anymore, since you worked so hard.

339
00:48:38,918 --> 00:48:43,618
試行錯誤っちにおいで もうずっと本能的に気持ちいいだけの
Come on over here, and enjoy yourself

340
00:48:43,918 --> 00:48:47,118
ゴールを見せてあげる
in a purely instinctual bliss forever!

341
00:48:48,118 --> 00:48:51,118
窮境極まってこそ光るカタルシス
Catharsis shines brightest at the height of extremity,

342
00:48:51,318 --> 00:48:54,618
もういっちょ因果律リセットで 魂デトックス
and detox your soul with one more law-of-cause-and-effect reset!

343
00:49:04,118 --> 00:49:13,118
いつかの、あったかもしれない世界の出来事までも、この冥界ではこうして思念として漂っているんだね。
Even the events of a world that might have once existed are drifting as thoughts here in the Underworld...

344
00:49:13,618 --> 00:49:19,118
あまり深入りしてはいけないよ、こういうのが一番たちが悪い。
You shouldn't delve too deeply into them; these are the worst kind.

345
00:49:19,618 --> 00:49:24,118
私はただ、あなたを愛していただけ。
I was only loving you...

346
00:49:32,118 --> 00:49:38,618
物言わぬ唇に息を吹き込んで、
Breathing life into silent lips,

347
00:49:39,118 --> 00:49:45,618
今宵「あなた」は蘇る あの頃の姿で。
tonight "you" are resurrected in your appearance from back then.

348
00:49:49,618 --> 00:49:53,618
[Title: ネクロの花嫁]
[Title: Necro no Hanayome]

349
00:50:11,446 --> 00:50:16,076
白銀の娘が誓いをした。この身体あなたに捧げるわ
The silver-haired maiden made a vow. "I offer this body to you."

350
00:50:16,446 --> 00:50:19,946
白服の医者が囁いた。「迎えに行くよ」
The doctor in white robes whispered, "I'm coming to get you."

351
00:50:20,446 --> 00:50:24,746
白銀の娘は朽ち果てた。世界のだれにも見捨てられ
The silver-haired maiden withered away, forsaken by everyone in the world.

352
00:50:24,946 --> 00:50:30,746
白服の医者は憐れんで、誰も知らない隠し場所で眠らせた
The doctor in white robes took pity and let her sleep in a hidden place known to no one.

353
00:50:31,046 --> 00:50:37,346
朽ちてなお美しく青色で、ふたりしかない霊廟で
Still beautiful even in decay, in an azure, solitary mausoleum...

354
00:50:37,546 --> 00:50:40,646
医者は恋をした
The doctor fell in love.

355
00:50:40,946 --> 00:50:46,346
それは永遠の恋か。禁断の行為か。
Is this eternal love? Is it a forbidden act?

356
00:50:46,846 --> 00:50:52,646
また逢いたいと願うだけ。それが罪なのでしょうか。
Wishing only to meet again... is that a sin?

357
00:50:52,946 --> 00:50:58,446
物言わぬ唇に生気を吹き込んで、
Breathing life into those silent lips...

358
00:50:58,746 --> 00:51:03,946
今宵ふたりは結ばれる。祝福もされずに。
Tonight the two shall be joined, without even a blessing.

359
00:51:15,946 --> 00:51:21,646
拘束衣で嵌め合い青いガラスを、破りかけた腕に切る笑いを
Blue glass locked in straitjackets, slicing smiles into trembling arms...

360
00:51:21,946 --> 00:51:27,446
犯された内臓に縫うガーゼを、宝飾で飾った白いドレスを
Gauze sewing into violated innards, a white dress adorned with jewels...

361
00:51:27,746 --> 00:51:33,746
朽ちゆくたび取り繕って、恋を歌って、また医者は
Patching her up each time she decays, singing of love, the doctor...

362
00:51:33,946 --> 00:51:39,446
手を染め続けた
Continued to stain his hands.

363
00:52:02,946 --> 00:52:08,446
やがて暴かれたのは見にくい怪物で、それを創り上げた医者は弁解を叫んだ
What was eventually exposed was an ugly monster, and the doctor who created it cried out in defense...

364
00:52:15,946 --> 00:52:21,446
「これは永遠の恋だ。彼女の願望だ。」
"This is eternal love. It is her desire."

365
00:52:21,746 --> 00:52:27,446
死にゆくと決めたお前らが、見棄てた女じゃないか
"Isn't she the woman you abandoned, you who chose to die?"

366
00:52:27,746 --> 00:52:33,346
嗚呼……哀しき花嫁。物言えぬままで、
Ah... sorrowful bride. Remaining unable to speak,

367
00:52:33,746 --> 00:52:39,446
今宵ふたりは裁かれる。彼女を見棄てた人達の正義で
Tonight the two are judged, by the justice of the people who abandoned her.

368
00:52:39,746 --> 00:52:45,446
正しいのはだれ？
Who is in the right?

